    "POST /announcements/blog::blog.create": "Blog's only foreign key is userId, set from req.user.id. A session-derived id cannot dangle, and the model carries no unique constraint.",
    "POST /announcements/global-notice::globalNotice.create": "GlobalNotice's only foreign key is createdById, set from req.user.id. A session-derived id cannot dangle, and the model carries no unique constraint.",
    "POST /forums/{id}/catchup::forumLastReadTopic.upsert": "No client-supplied id reaches a constrained column: userId is session-derived, and forumTopicId/forumPostId come from a forumTopic read issued in the same request. #564 is about a well-formed request naming something absent; here the caller names nothing. A topic deleted concurrently mid-transaction is a different concern and would not be a client error.",
    "POST /auth::userSession.create": "The only foreign key is userId, taken from the account just authenticated in this request, so it cannot dangle.",
    "POST /messages/drafts::pmDraft.create": "The only foreign key is userId, from the session. `toUserId` is a plain Int with no relation, so it cannot raise P2003.",
    "POST /messages/mass::massMessage.create": "The only foreign key is senderId, from the session.",
    "POST /posts::post.create": "The only foreign key is userId, from the session; Post carries no unique constraint.",
    "POST /site-history::siteHistory.create": "The only foreign key is authorId, from the session; SiteHistory carries no unique constraint.",
    "DELETE /profile::user.update": "Addressed by req.user.id — the row belongs to the caller's own live session, so it is present by construction.",
    "POST /install::userSettings.create": "Created inside the install transaction with no foreign key set and no unique constraint on the model.",
    "POST /install::user.create": "Its three foreign keys (userRankId, userSettingsId, profileId) are all rows created earlier in the same transaction. The unique username/email are client-supplied, but the route refuses with 409 unless settings.installedAt is null, so there is no existing user for them to collide with.",
    "src/lib/audit.ts::audit::auditLog.create": "AuditLog's only foreign key is actorId, and every caller passes an id that cannot dangle: req.user.id, the resolved system actor (resolveSystemActorId), or, in ratioPolicy.ts, the subject's own id as that actor's fallback. Traced across every audit() call on 2026-09-29 (#596, ADR-0048). The model carries no unique constraint."
